BlitzMax.LSP provides reusable JSON-RPC framing and a BlitzMax Language Server
Protocol implementation.

#TLspTransport reads and writes standard `Content-Length` framed UTF-8 messages over
BlitzMax streams. #TBlitzMaxLspServer owns document and workspace state and dispatches
requests to the services built on #BlitzMax.Language.

An executable language-server host can create a transport for its input and output
streams and pass it to #TBlitzMaxLspServer.Run. An application with its own message
loop may instead pass individual JSON payloads to #HandlePayload and write the
returned responses itself.

The module also exposes small JSON-RPC construction helpers such as #JsonResponse,
#JsonErrorResponse, and #JsonNotification.

Consumers that need syntax trees, semantic models, diagnostics, or source navigation
without the LSP protocol should use #BlitzMax.Language directly.
